Subject: [PATCH] assay-statusgen: reconcile lifecycle cells from PR history

STAGED, NOT APPLIED. This patch is the reconcile step the brief-v2 migration's
release note tells every adopter to add to the workflow that regenerates their
board. It is committed as a .patch file rather than applied because the identity
that opened the flag-day pull request cannot write under .github/workflows/ —
that scope is deliberately withheld from it. Whoever holds the workflows scope
applies it:

    git apply .github/assay-statusgen.reconcile.patch
    git rm  .github/assay-statusgen.reconcile.patch

WHAT IT DOES. Under brief-v2 a brief's lifecycle cell is DERIVED, not asserted:
statusgen reads it back from the `Brief:` trailer on the pull requests that
touched each brief. `statusgen reconcile --backfill` performs that fold and
needs one authenticated read of pull-request history, so it runs in the regen
job — after the board is regenerated and before the result is committed.

WHY THE TOKEN IS THE DEFAULT ONE. The step only READS pull requests. The regen
job already mints a write-scoped App token for its push; that token is not
reused here, so a read stays a read.

UNTIL IT IS APPLIED the authoring columns regenerate normally and the lifecycle
columns are carried through unchanged rather than reconciled — the board stays
correct, it simply does not yet fold in what the pull-request history says.

--- a/.github/workflows/assay-statusgen.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/assay-statusgen.yml
@@
     permissions:
       contents: read
+      pull-requests: read
     steps:
@@
       - name: Regenerate STATUS.md
         run: |
           "${RUNNER_TEMP}/statusgen" --root .
+      - name: Reconcile lifecycle cells from PR history
+        run: |
+          "${RUNNER_TEMP}/statusgen" reconcile --backfill --root .
+        env:
+          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
       - name: Commit STATUS.md if it changed
